{"id":"7822cf72-8846-401c-a6ce-a91a3f8f6011","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.019","title":"Multimodal single-cell epigenomic and 3D genome atlas of the human basal ganglia","title_zh":"人类基底神经节多模态单细胞表观基因组和三维基因组图谱","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.019","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.10.019","abstract":"The basal ganglia (BG) underlie motor control, reward processing, and many neurological and psychiatric disorders, yet cell-type-resolved epigenomic and 3D genome maps of the human BG remain limited. Here, we present a multimodal single-cell atlas of DNA methylation (261,331 nuclei) and 3D chromatin conformation (229,286 nuclei) from eight subregions, harmonized under the BG consensus taxonomy and integrated with matched data across multiple regulatory layers. We identify millions of differentially methylated regions across cell types, enriched for distinct transcription factor motifs, and link them to disease-associated heritability. We characterize the POU6F2+ STR D2 SMYD2-HTR7 spiny projection neuron (SPN) subtype, with concordant signatures across multiple modalities, and reveal region-specific methylation and contact gradients. Integrative gene regulatory networks (GRNs) predict cell-type-resolved enhancer-promoter interactions, nominating candidate regulatory mechanisms for Parkinson's disease (PD) risk variants at SNCA. Finally, multiplexed error-robust fluorescence in situ hybridization (MERFISH) profiling combined with cross-species Patch-seq identifies a neuronal subtype, STR FS PTHLH-PVALB GABA, with electrophysiological differences across the striatal matrix-striosome (MS) boundary.","abstract_zh":"基底神经节（BG）参与运动控制、奖赏处理以及许多神经和精神疾病，但人类基底神经节的细胞类型分辨表观基因组和三维基因组图谱仍然有限。在此，我们呈现来自八个亚区的多模态单细胞图谱，包括DNA甲基化（261,331个细胞核）和三维染色质构象（229,286个细胞核），在基底神经节共识分类学下协调，并与多个调控层面的匹配数据整合。我们鉴定了数百万个细胞类型间的差异甲基化区域，这些区域富集了不同的转录因子基序，并将其与疾病相关的遗传力相关联。我们描述了POU6F2+ STR D2 SMYD2-HTR7棘质投影神经元（SPN）亚型，在多个模态中具有一致的特征，并揭示了区域特异性的甲基化和接触梯度。整合基因调控网络（GRN）预测了细胞类型分辨的增强子-启动子相互作用，提名了SNCA处帕金森病（PD）风险变异的候选调控机制。最后，多重抗错荧光原位杂交（MERFISH）分析结合跨物种Patch-seq，鉴定出一种神经元亚型STR FS PTHLH-PVALB GABA，其在纹状体基质-丝体（MS）边界处存在电生理差异。","snippet":"The basal ganglia (BG) underlie motor control, reward processing, and many neurological and psychiatric disorders, yet cell-type-resolved epigenomic and 3D genome maps of the human BG remain limited. Here, we present a multimodal single-cell atlas of DNA methylation (261,331 nuclei) and 3D chromatin conformation (229,286 nuclei) from eight subregions, harmonized under the BG consensus taxonomy and integrated with ma…","translated_at":"2026-11-14T08:11:26.352478Z","translation_model":"nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"23","published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date":"2026-11-12T23:34:37Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-11-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Wubin Ding","authors_text":"Wubin Ding, Amit Klein, Cindy Tatiana Báez-Becerra, Jonathan A. Rink, Anna Bartlett, Ruoxuan Wang, Qiurui Zeng, Rosa Gomez Castanon, Joseph R. Nery, Emma Osgood, William Owens, Alaina Petrella, Chumo Chen, Andrea Saldaña Acerbo, Ariana S. Barcoma, Jiayi Liu, Kaitlyn G. Russo, Kyle W. Knutson, Carissa K. Young, Jackson K. Willier, Cesar Barragan, Jessica Arzavala, Silvia Cho, Jordan Altshul, Derek Chan, Eshaan Soma, Jammy Luo, Manya Jain, Sarah Velazquez, Guha V. Sundaram, Austin C. Manning, Yareli Sanchez, Aleksandra Bikkina, Yuanyuan Fu, Kaushik Komandur, Ethan Doan, Shuai Fu, Carolyn O’Connor, Michelle Liem, Mikayla V. Marrin, Cynthia Rose, Shane N. Alt, Jillian Berry, Joseph Colin Kern, Eric Boone, Wei Tian, Huamin Chen, Yang Xie, Yue Wu, Manoj Hariharan, Kai Li, Lei Chang, Nelson Johansen, Wenjin Zhang, Zoey Zhao, Jesus Flores, Chu-Yi Tai, Jacqueline Olness, Natalie Schenker-Ahmed, Xiao-Ping Liu, Quan Zhu, Brian E. Kalmbach, Rebecca D. Hodge, Trygve E. Bakken, Ed S. Lein, Daofeng Li, T